cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "markov-chain-monte-carlo: A composable MCMC framework for Rust"
version: "0.2.0"
url: "https://github.com/acgetchell/markov-chain-monte-carlo"
repository-code: "https://github.com/acgetchell/markov-chain-monte-carlo"
authors:
  - family-names: "Getchell"
    given-names: "Adam"
    email: "adam@adamgetchell.org"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0797-0021"
keywords:
  - "markov-chain-monte-carlo"
  - "mcmc"
  - "metropolis-hastings"
  - "monte-carlo"
  - "sampling"
abstract: >-
  markov-chain-monte-carlo is a Rust library providing composable
  Metropolis-Hastings sampling over arbitrary state spaces, with clone-based
  and in-place proposal models, log-space transition handling, rollback on
  invalid proposal states, seeded reproducibility, and ergonomic sampler
  utilities.
